/*--------------------------------*- Choupo -*--------------------------------*\
  Zn-Br: mean ionic activity coefficient gamma_pm and osmotic coefficient
  phi of the salt (Zn)1(Br)2 in water at 298.15 K -- the EVALUATED
  (recommended) values of
    R. N. Goldberg, Evaluated Activity and Osmotic Coefficients for Aqueous Solutions: Bi-Univalent Compounds of Zinc, Cadmium, and Ethylene Bis(Trimethylammonium) Chloride and Iodide, J. Phys. Chem. Ref. Data 10 (1981) 1-55,
    doi:10.1063/1.555639, the ZnBr2 table of recommended values, p. 22 (m, gamma, phi, a_w).
  The evaluation is the primary source of these recommended values (its
  own references are the measurements behind them).
  TRANSCRIBED 2026-11-11 (DEV.md 4c C311) from the NIST reprint
  (nist-jpcrd-1.555639.pdf): every row read by eye from the page image; phi checked against the printed water activity (ln a_w = -nu m phi M_w, to 2.5e-4) and gamma against its neighbours by the Gibbs-Duhem relation.
  Rows kept: 0.1 mol/kg up to ionic strength 6 mol/kg; a row the
  source marks saturated, supersaturated or from another author is not
  here.  Every 4th row (0-based index % 4 == 3, never the first or the
  last) is HELD OUT by the case (system/propsDict), not by this file.
\*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
provenance
{
    source        "R. N. Goldberg, Evaluated Activity and Osmotic Coefficients for Aqueous Solutions: Bi-Univalent Compounds of Zinc, Cadmium, and Ethylene Bis(Trimethylammonium) Chloride and Iodide, J. Phys. Chem. Ref. Data 10 (1981) 1-55";
    doi           "10.1063/1.555639";
    location      "the ZnBr2 table of recommended values, p. 22 (m, gamma, phi, a_w)";
    reviewStatus  transcribed;
}

temperature 298.15;   // K, every row

columns
(
    { name m;     unit mol/kg; }
    { name gamma; unit -; }       // gamma_pm, molality scale
    { name phi;   unit -; }       // molal osmotic coefficient
);

data
(
    0.1     0.5531   0.8749  
    0.2     0.5152   0.8877  
    0.3     0.5064   0.9117  
    0.4     0.5088   0.9383  
    0.5     0.5162   0.9636  
    0.6     0.5254   0.9859  
    0.7     0.5348   1.0044  
    0.8     0.5436   1.0192  
    0.9     0.5513   1.0303  
    1       0.5578   1.0383  
    1.25    0.5686   1.0478  
    1.5     0.5738   1.048   
    1.75    0.5762   1.0449  
    2       0.578    1.0423  
);
